# The build context is the repository ROOT for every service, including
# apps/web (see CLAUDE.md), so anything here is a candidate for a layer.
#
# The entry that matters is deploy/k8s/secrets.yaml: it is the filled-in,
# gitignored copy of secrets.example.yaml and holds live production credentials
# (Postgres password, MinIO secret key, JWT signing key, OIDC state secret, the
# TLS private key). .gitignore keeps it out of git; this keeps it out of images.
#
# No current Dockerfile does `COPY . .` — they all copy go.work, packages/,
# apps/<service>/ and the package manifests explicitly — so nothing leaks today.
# This file exists so that a future `COPY . .` is not a credential disclosure.
deploy/k8s/secrets.yaml
*.key
*.pem

# Not needed in any build, and .worktrees/ in particular can contain whole
# second checkouts (including their own secrets.yaml).
.git
.worktrees
node_modules
dist
.cache
bin
